{
  "summary": "Updates the test framework's P2PConnection v1 message parser to verify network magic bytes only after receiving a full 24-byte header, matching bitcoind's V1Transport behavior. Previously, the test framework rejected the stream after receiving only 4 bytes if they did not match the magic.",
  "problem": "If network socket data arrives in small chunks, P2PConnection could disconnect after reading 4 bytes. Because bitcoind's V2Transport::ShouldReconnectV1 only attempts a v1 reconnect if at least a full 24-byte header was sent before peer disconnection, premature disconnection causes the node not to reconnect, leading p2p_v2_encrypted.py to time out.",
  "evidence": [
    "Author notes the failure is reproducible under forced chunked socket sends: \"This was found -- and can be reproduced -- by using a reproducer patch, that forces all socket sends to use smaller chunking. For the run with the reproducer see #36724.\"",
    "Related to issue #36726 regarding test errors from socket data chunking assumptions."
  ],
