  "card": "Updates P2PConnection in the Python test framework to wait for the complete 24-byte v1 header before validating magic bytes, mirroring bitcoind's V1Transport::readHeader. Currently, if socket reads are chunked in pieces under 24 bytes, P2PConnection disconnects too early, preventing bitcoind from triggering its v2-to-v1 downgrade fallback and causing p2p_v2_encrypted.py to hang or time out. Author demonstrated the failure using a forced-chunking reproducer in PR #36724.",
